            <ArticleTitle>Bone Marrow Aspirate Concentrate and Its Uses in the Foot and Ankle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-26</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0891-8422(17)30087-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cpm.2017.08.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bone marrow aspirate has been used for the adjunctive treatment of numerous pathologic conditions in orthopedics. Viable cells are found in aspiration from many different anatomic regions of the body. Concentration of these cells has been shown to improve healing due to the increased number of certain important cells. This article discusses the mechanisms involved and reviews the literature.</AbstractText>
